-- title:
--   Killing an element of tsetminust² in a truncated polynomial algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field and let $N, M$ be natural numbers. Write $A_{N+1} := \mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,(N+1))\,k$, a polynomial algebra in $N+1$ variables over $k$, and let $\mathfrak m \subseteq A_{N+1}$ be the kernel of the constant-term homomorphism `MvPolynomial.constantCoeff` $: A_{N+1} \to k$, i.e. the ideal generated by the variables. Set $T_{N+1} := A_{N+1}/\mathfrak m^{M+1}$ and let $\mathfrak t \subseteq T_{N+1}$ be the image of $\mathfrak m$ under the quotient map, that is, $\mathrm{Ideal.map}$ of $\mathfrak m$ along `Ideal.Quotient.mk`. Let $x \in T_{N+1}$ satisfy the two hypotheses $x \in \mathfrak t$ and $x \notin \mathfrak t^2$. The conclusion asserts that the type of $k$-algebra isomorphisms from $T_{N+1}/(x)$, the quotient of $T_{N+1}$ by the ideal generated by the single element $x$, to $T_N := \mathrm{MvPolynomial}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,N)\,k$ modulo the $(M+1)$-st power of the kernel of its own constant-term homomorphism, is nonempty; so such an isomorphism exists, with no particular choice of it recorded.
--
--   This is the "surplus variable" step in normalising a presentation of a truncated (artinian local) polynomial algebra: dividing out one element of the maximal ideal that is not in its square lowers the number of variables by one while keeping the truncation degree $M+1$. It is used in [`Algebra.exists_ker_eq_span_of_surjective_truncated_of_ker_eq_span`](thm.html#Algebra.exists_ker_eq_span_of_surjective_truncated_of_ker_eq_span), and its proof invokes the truncated inverse-function statement [`MvPolynomial.bijective_algHom_truncated_of_forall_exists_sub_mem_sq`](thm.html#MvPolynomial.bijective_algHom_truncated_of_forall_exists_sub_mem_sq), by which a $k$-algebra endomorphism of a truncated polynomial algebra sending each variable to an element congruent to it modulo $\mathfrak t^2$ is bijective.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPolynomial_nonempty_truncated_quotient_span_singleton_algEquiv_truncated_of_not_mem_sq.lean

